/-!
# Sites given by families of coverings, continuous functors and morphisms of sites

A site in the sense of Stacks 00VH is a category `C` together with a set `Cov(C)` of *indexed*
families of morphisms with fixed target `{U_i → U}_{i ∈ I}`, closed under isomorphisms,
composition and base change, where the fibre products needed for base change are required to
exist only for the members of coverings. This file records that notion as `Stacks.Sites.Site`,
with the covering families kept as indexed families (`CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover`), and
defines, for such sites, continuous functors (Stacks 00WV) and morphisms of sites (Stacks 00X1).

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Sites.Site`: a site in the sense of Stacks 00VH.
* `Stacks.Sites.Site.IsContinuous`: a continuous functor between sites (Stacks 00WV): it carries
  coverings to coverings, with the same index set, and for every covering `{V_i → V}` and every
  `T → V` the canonical morphism `u(T ×_V V_i) → u(T) ×_{u(V)} u(V_i)` is an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.Sites.Site.topology`: the Grothendieck topology whose sheaves are the sheaves on the
  site, i.e. the one generated by the coverings.
* `Stacks.Sites.Site.IsMorphismOfSites`: a morphism of sites `f : D → C` (Stacks 00X1), given by
  a continuous functor `u : C ⥤ D` such that `u_s : G ↦ (u_p G)^#` is exact.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.Site.isSheaf_topology_iff`: a presheaf is a sheaf for `Site.topology` exactly when
  it satisfies the sheaf condition for every covering of the site.

## Implementation notes

The axioms of a site are stated exactly as in Stacks 00VH together with its clarifications.
In axiom (1) the required covering is one whose index set is a singleton and whose unique morphism
is the given isomorphism; this is phrased as a covering with subsingleton index type whose set of
arrows is `{f}`. In axiom (2) the composite family `{V_{ij} → U}_{i ∈ I, j ∈ J_i}` is indexed by
the dependent pairs `(i, j)`, which is `PreZeroHypercover.bind`. In axiom (3) the fibre products
`U_i ×_U V` exist, and the family of second projections is a covering *for some choice* of the
fibre products: a family of pullback squares is given, and the family of its projections to `V`
lies in `Cov(C)`. No fibre products other than these are assumed, so `C` need not have pullbacks.

Clause (2) of Stacks 00WV involves `T ×_V V_i` in `C`, which exists by axiom (3) of `C`, and
`u(T) ×_{u(V)} u(V_i)` in `D`, which exists by axiom (3) of `D` applied to the covering
`{u(V_i) → u(V)}` of clause (1). The structure `Site.IsContinuous` therefore states clause (2)
after clause (1), using the instances `Site.hasPullback` that these axioms provide; the morphism
of clause (2) is Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Limits.pullbackComparison`.

The sheaves on a site are the presheaves of sets satisfying the sheaf condition for every
covering (Stacks 00VL). The coverings of a site form a `CategoryTheory.Coverage` (axiom (3) gives
its pullback condition), and a presheaf is a sheaf for the Grothendieck topology this coverage
generates exactly when it satisfies the sheaf condition for every covering
(`CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheaf_coverage`). So `Sh(C)` is `Sheaf S.topology (Type u)`, and the
functor `u_s` of Stacks 00WX is `CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafPullbackConstruction.sheafPullback`,
which is by definition the restriction to sheaves of the left Kan extension `u_p` along `u.op`
followed by sheafification. Exactness of a functor is preservation of finite limits and of finite
colimits. As in `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsMorphismOfSites`, the categories of a morphism of sites
are small and the sheaves take values in sets of the same universe, so that `u_p` and
sheafification exist.

The existing `StacksContinuousFunctor.IsContinuous` (sites given by pretopologies, with the
pushforward *sieve* in place of the image family) and `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsMorphismOfSites`
(built on Mathlib's `Functor.IsContinuous`, i.e. on the conclusion of Stacks 00WW rather than on
Stacks continuity) are not Stacks' notions; the definitions here are.

